Neon spaces: every space is a container (M5).

The default storage partition is no longer a space. A new profile starts with
one container-backed space, "Personal"; the default space of an older profile
becomes a space with a container of its own (renamed Personal if it still had
the name "Default"). Any space can be renamed, moved and deleted except the
last one, in the switcher row, the edit bubble and the settings page.

New tabs get a space's container whenever the profile has spaces, in every
layout and with a single space; the pager, hiding and switching still need two
spaces in the vertical layout. A tab whose page lands outside every space's
container (a tab of an older profile, a container that no space uses, a
restored tab whose container is gone) is reopened by its URL in its space, at
its place; an extension page in such a tab moves to the global window.
Nothing is copied out of the default partition.

With a single space the switcher row stays hidden, so the New Tab button's
context menu gets "New space" (command id 39520).

